#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
W3 Linux Mod Manager: a small Witcher 3 mod manager for Linux (Proton / Wine).

How it works
- Archives get extracted and sorted into a staging area inside the game folder:
      <game>/_ModManager/data/staging/<mod-id>/{mods,dlc,bin}/...
- Enabled mods are deployed into the game folder as hardlinks (same disk, so
  instant and no extra space). Falls back to copying if hardlinks fail.
- Each mod that clashes has a priority number (1 wins), kept apart from its place in the
  list. Written to mods.settings inside the prefix so the game actually respects it.
- Any game file a mod would overwrite (e.g. a vanilla bin/ xml) gets backed up
  and restored when that mod is disabled or removed.
- Menu xmls are added to dx11filelist.txt / dx12filelist.txt automatically.
- Paths are matched case-insensitively, so "Mods/" and "mods/" never end up
  as two separate folders (Wine would get confused).

Needs: PyQt6.   For .7z / .rar also: 7zip (7zz / 7z) or bsdtar.
"""

